          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "-: Welcome to another course module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 6.54,
          "en": "Welcome to this course module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.54,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "We already learned a lot about Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "and thus far we really built a single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "We used directives and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "to change portions of this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 21.36,
          "en": "but in the end, we always were on the same page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "If you looked at the URL at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "it was always local host 4200.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "Now, what if you wanted to have a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "where you actually display several pages?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "Like you have a /users or a /accounts page?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 37.95,
          "en": "Now, you might think that for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.95,
          "end": 39.96,
          "en": "you indeed need multiple pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "multiple index html files or something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "but you don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "Angular ships with its own router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 52.29,
          "en": "which allows you to change the URL in the URL bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.29,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "and still only use one page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "but then exchange major parts or a lot of parts of that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "so that to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "it really looks like a new page was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "because maybe only the header is the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "but behind the scenes, it is still JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 74.28,
          "en": "changing a lot of parts in your DOM in your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "making it look like a new page was rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "but you're still in the Angular world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "in your single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
